## The two defects

1. The fork read as an open hand that held the nest. Two short prongs, one on each side of the
   nest, each with a round leaf cap. The caps looked like two mittens. The line art showed this
   most clearly.
2. The trunk base read as a pole on a stand. The root flare was a flat round disc on the ground.

Where they show: `out/storytime/l2/unit1/w01/rows/l2-w01-story-page-a-nest-and-a-nut-v4.png`,
`l2-w01-story-page-a-nest-and-a-nut-line-v4.png`, and `l2-w01-story-page-a-nest-v5.png`.

## What changed (assets/storytime-low-branch.ts only)

- The branch dips, then splits into a long outer twig and a short steeper back twig. The twigs
  differ in length, angle, and thickness. Neither ends in a round cap.
- The leaf caps are gone from the twigs by the seat. One joined arc of soft leaf clusters runs
  from the back twig, over the fork, to the outer twig tip. Each cluster touches its neighbour
  and a twig, so no leaf floats. The arc sits behind the nest (z at or below -0.14 m) and above
  the rim.
- The wide flat flare is gone. Four short roots of different sizes sink below the ground plane.
- Kept: the round crown (about 0.77 m), the thick taper (0.16 m at the base), the warm bark, the
  fresh green leaves, the Chibi Sprouts soft rounds, and the branch toward +X.
- `NEST_SEAT` keeps its name and value: x 0.50 m, y 0.70 m, z 0.04 m. The branch tail and the
  saddle top sit at y = 0.704 m, so the nest rests on wood. Every point of both twigs stays
  outside the nest footprint. No text, letter, number, logo, face, or carved mark.
- No single leaves. No flat disc or ring at the base.

